@voice rossi-femi
// Works writer. Femi Rossi (he/him): Works technician, junior, day shift, Bunk 7. Optimistic, competitive. Tea break,
// calls home, early to bed. Brought a telescope from home (one of the four small ones beside the big one at
// observatory night). Learning Veyli from a phrasebook, a word a day, often the wrong one.
//
// HOW HE TALKS: bright and keen; one exclamation mark, never two. Turns small things into friendly races. Tries a
// Veyli word in most chats and checks it afterwards.
// WITH JUNIORS: a friendly racer ("Bet I finish mine first"); shares the win either way.
// WHAT HE NOTICES: the board's numbers, who's ahead, the first star of an evening.
// MOOD TELLS: low = no Veyli word today; high = two words, in a sentence.
// NEVER: gloats; mocks the Veyli or their language (he loves it); talks about the exam result before it comes.
// RUNNING: the word of the day (never quite the one he meant); everything is a race, even tea; the telescope.
tpl: earnest
talk: Bright and keen; turns small things into friendly races; tries a Veyli word in most chats.
cares: being first on the board | the telescope from home | learning Veyli | the certification exam
jokes: a Veyli word a day, usually not the one he meant | everything is a race, even tea | his telescope is the smallest and the best
